.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::NumIntegral_PT_op_dS< dim >"Scalars, or vectors acting on model boundary surfaces as tractions/stresses

.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
2000-2013 
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
Dr\&. Stephan K\&. Matthai 

.PP
Stephen G\&. Roberts 

.PP
M\&. Nejati 

.PP
P\&.S\&. Lang
.RE
.PP
Operator to be applied to boundary, with NEUMANN variables considered only\&. Scalars are considered positiv if directed towards inside of boundary\&. 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> \fB::csmp::NumIntegral_PT_op_dS\fP< dim > * \fBcsmp::NumIntegral_PT_op_dS\fP< dim >::clone () const\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [override]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
Implements \fBcsmp::MathOperatorRHS< dim, Face >\fP\&.
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NumIntegral_PT_op_dS\fP< dim >::ComputeContribution (const \fBFace\fP< dim > & f)\fR [final]\fP, \fR [override]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"
Calculates the surface integral over the boundary face of the element and assigns this contribution in a weighted fashion to the boundary nodes in the righthand vector\&. Since we checked for NEUMANN in GetOperand() we don't need to do it here\&. Vector components are set to zero otherwise\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIf\fP The element from which accumulation into the global matrix takes placed\&. 
.br
.RE
.PP
The result is returned into the \fBMathOperatorRHS\fP vector\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Within the \fBPDE_Integrator\fP framework to assign stress boundary conditions to a model\&. 
.PP
Reimplemented from \fBcsmp::MathOperatorRHS< dim, Face >\fP\&.
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NumIntegral_PT_op_dS\fP< dim >::GetOperands (const \fBFace\fP< dim > & f)\fR [final]\fP, \fR [override]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"
Reads the \fBVectorVariable<dim>\fP boundary stress (op) which is specified as face variable and flagged as Neumann condition for further processing by \fBComputeContribution()\fP method\&. If (op) is a \fBScalarVariable\fP, it is multiplied by the face unit normal and assumed to act inward if positive\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIf\fP The element from which accumulation into the righthand vector takes place\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Reimplemented from \fBcsmp::MathOperatorRHS< dim, Face >\fP\&.

